# Optional: point Jetty at the RTSP helper HTTP API (default: use Vite dev proxy paths /jetty-live-stream).
# Local dev: start the helper with `npm run dev:stream` or `npm run dev:jetty-live` from repo root (see Docs/Plan/LOCAL-DEV.md).
# Example direct URL:
# VITE_JETTY_LIVE_HTTP_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:3080
#
# Optional WebSocket port when using direct origin (health JSON may override).
# VITE_JETTY_LIVE_WS_PORT=9999
#
# Optional: show legacy plan-based Vessel Pipeline on Dashboard (Actuals pipeline is always shown; rebuild required).
# VITE_USE_LEGACY_VESSEL_PIPELINE=true
#
# Downstream Hub analytics SDK. Both URL and key are required; leave unset to keep the SDK off.
# Key is publishable (it ships in the page) but environment-specific. Do not reuse another app's key.
# The Hub must allow this browser origin or collect calls return 403.
# VITE_HUB_SDK_URL=http://test-dwshub.kpndomain.com/api/sdk/v1/hub-sdk.js
# VITE_HUB_SDK_KEY=
# VITE_HUB_SDK_DEBUG=true
# VITE_GIT_SHA=
